## Task

1. Write every `files[]` entry per its `content_outline`, following the
   type conventions in `{{ input.__task.source_folder }}/../../references/`.
2. SKILL.md for `workflow` and `flow`: render the scaffold, do not
   hand-compose it:
   ```bash
   SIFU_TPL={{ input.__task.source_folder }}/../../templates/skill
   ~/.kiro/skills/home/template/scripts/render.sh \
       --template "$SIFU_TPL/<type>.md.j2" \
       --include-dir "$SIFU_TPL" \
       --include-dir ~/.kiro/skills/home/loomv2/templates \
       --json-vars /tmp/{{ input.design.frontmatter.name }}-skill-vars.json \
       > '{{ input.skill_dir }}/SKILL.md'
   ```
   The template header lists its variables.
3. Workflow:
   ```bash
   LOOM={{ input.__loom.runtime }}
   ```
   Create task folders with `$LOOM task new <name> --loom-root <root>`,
   write `io.yaml` and the body file, run `$LOOM task io-python` for
   `tool.py` tasks, `chmod +x` every `tool.sh`, then validate every
   graph file:
   ```bash
   for g in '{{ input.skill_dir }}'/loom*/graph*.yaml; do
       $LOOM validate '{{ input.skill_dir }}' --graph "$g"
   done
   ```
   Fix and re-run until exit 0; after 3 failed attempts,
   `$LOOM runtime fail` with the last error.
4. Script packages: `uv lock` in each `pyproject.toml` folder.

## Output

```bash
LOOM={{ input.__loom.runtime }}
WD={{ input.__loom.workdir }}
$LOOM output init "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}'
$LOOM output add "$WD" --task '{{ input.__task.id }}' \
    --set 'files[].path={{ input.skill_dir }}/SKILL.md' \
    --set 'files[-1].action=created'
```

One `files[]` entry per file written.
